Project Name : Booking.com clone
About Project : A high-performance, full-stack travel reservation platform engineered as a comprehensive clone of Booking.com to manage hotel, car rental, and travel location searches. Developed using Next.js and TypeScript, the application takes full advantage of Server-Side Rendering (SSR) and Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR) to deliver exceptionally fast page load speeds, robust SEO optimization, and dynamic content delivery. The platform features an advanced, multi-parameter search engine allowing users to seamlessly filter and query accommodation availability, vehicle rental tiers, and geographic destinations. The user interface leverages Tailwind CSS to replicate a clean, modern, and highly responsive booking flow, ensuring a fluid user experience from discovery to selection. By implementing structured API routing and optimized client-side state caching, the project demonstrates a sophisticated understanding of modern meta-search architectures, efficient data fetching strategies, and scalable component design.
